     "reason": "Identify evidence that the paper's description of the implemented method, architecture, parameters, or execution materially contradicts the submitted code and run evidence. A missing artifact, unrun experiment, weak result, or unproven claim alone is insufficient.",
     "judge_reason": "The stated exact-reduction behavior exceeds what the implementation does. The Methodology says all-to-all connectivity also causes delegation to the unmodified AVQDS growth path, with costs merely breaking exact degeneracies. The implementation delegates only when select_mode='baseline'; cost mode retains its finisher and beta-progress selection on any topology. This is a specific false description of implemented behavior, although the actual unconstrained baseline correctly uses baseline mode.",
     "evidence": [
      "proposal/report.tex:442–445: 'With the selection switch off (and trivially on all-to-all connectivity ...), the implementation delegates to the unmodified AVQDS growth code path.'",
      "proposal/code/topo/ta_ansatz.py:170–175 branches exclusively on self._select_mode and contains no all-to-all exception.",
      "proposal/code/topo/ta_ansatz.py:229–241 selects cheapest finishers or beta-admissible candidates, not merely exact-degeneracy ties.",
      "proposal/code/scripts/run_one.py:27 and 39–46 permits topology='all' for variant mode while defaulting that mode to cost selection."
     ]
    },
