     "judge_reason": "The paper materially misdescribes the executed routing pattern by asserting that all four heavy-hex leaf edges carry rotations only. The audits show SWAPs on those edges in every headline topology-B run. For both LSM benchmarks, all nine SWAPs occur on leaf edges, directly contradicting the claimed pattern. The gates remain topology-compliant and their costs are counted.",
     "evidence": [
      "proposal/report.tex:762–770, especially :767–769: SWAP annotations are placed around the trunk, while 'the four leaf edges carry rotations only'; the same statement appears in report.pdf, pp. 9–10.",
      "proposal/code/topo/topology.py:10 defines leaf edges (0,1), (1,2), (4,5), and (6,7).",
      "proposal/logs/runs/variant_lsm_hzm07_B/audit.csv:7 and :9 record leaf-edge SWAPs; summing kind=swap records gives 3 on (1,2) and 6 on (4,5), all 9 SWAPs.",
